{"id":"u-7c9d8f2d-a871-43a0-9b74-d629176318d6","src":"community","title":"Opposites Attract: Superset Training","author":"Mithosphere","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/brf7o0-opposites-attract-superset-training","desc":"The Opposites Attract Workout is a comprehensive training protocol designed to maximize muscle size and strength by leveraging the power of antagonistic training and variable weekly structures. Instead of reserving supersets for small muscle groups like arms, this program builds an entire full-body routine out of a single, powerful concept.\n\nYour training weeks will alternate between heavy-duty straight-set training days and fast-paced, high-intensity superset or triset training days. By hitting every muscle fiber from every angle using a multi-faceted approach, you will accelerate your performance, trigger massive muscle pumps, and build a lasting foundation for total body thickness.\n\nTraining Principles & Layout\n\nTo balance recovery with optimal growth, each muscle group is targeted twice per week. The routine is divided into two distinct training styles:\n+ Round 1 (Days 1–3): Heavy-Duty Assault\n- Focus: Pure strength and progressive overload.\n- Execution: You will complete all sets and reps of an exercise, taking every working set near failure, before switching to an exercise for the opposing muscle group.\n- Rest: Rest 1.5 to 2.5 minutes between sets to maximize power.\n+ Round 2 (Days 4–6): High-Fatigue Performance\n- Focus: Extreme blood flow, metabolic stress, and massive muscle pumps.\n- Execution: Exercises grouped in supersets or trisets are performed back-to-back with minimal rest. You only rest after a full circuit is complete.\n- Rest: Rest 2 to 3 minutes between completed supersets and trisets.\n\nThe 7-Day Training Split\n+ Day 1 (Heavy) & Day 4 (Supersets): Quads, Hamstrings, Calves, Abs\n- Key movements: Squats, Leg Presses, Leg Curls, Extensions, Deadlifts, and Calf Raises.\n+ Day 2 (Heavy) & Day 5 (Supersets): Chest, Back, Traps\n- Key movements: Bench Press variations, Lat Pulldowns, Cable Rows, Shrugs, and Flyes.\n+ Day 3 (Heavy) & Day 6 (Supersets): Shoulders, Triceps, Biceps\n- Key movements: Standing Overhead Presses, Skull Crushers, Barbell Curls, and Lateral Raises.\n+ Day 7: Rest & Recovery\n\nWhy It Works\nTraditional routines that utilize the exact same setup every single workout can lead to stale training plateaus and diminished hormone release. By introducing alternating heavy and high-volume sessions, you constantly challenge your muscles with something new.\n\nThe heavy straight-set days boost testosterone and build foundational strength, allowing you to handle greater loads. The rapid-fire superset days supercharge your growth hormone response and improve your ability to handle volume at a fast pace. Together, they ensure no stone is left unturned on your path to building thick, functional muscle.","level":["Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":70,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-10-14T16:13:13.911Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["A: Quads, Hams, Calves & Abs","A: Chest, Back & Traps","A: Shoulders, Triceps & Biceps","B: Quads, Hams, Calves & Abs","B: Chest, Back & Traps","B: Shoulders, Triceps & Biceps"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"pct":70,"x":4}]},{"n":"Lying Leg Curl","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":9,"x":4}]},{"n":"Standing Calf Raise","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":9,"x":4}]},{"n":"Stiff Leg Deadlift","sets":[{"r":10,"pct":60,"x":3}]},{"n":"Seated Calf Raise","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Decline Crunch (Weighted)","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":9,"x":4}]},{"n":"Single Leg Extension","sets":[{"r":12,"rpe":9,"x":4}]},{"n":"Single-Leg Leg Curl","sets":[{"r":12,"rpe":9,"x":4}]},{"n":"Hanging Leg Raise","sets":[{"r":12,"rpe":9,"x":4}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"pct":70,"x":4}]},{"n":"Wide Grip Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":9,"x":4}]},{"n":"Shru